{
 "id": "pair_view",
 "label": "Pair View",
 "category": "Purrmiere",
 "version": 1,
 "blurb": "Named crop regions of one picture (two players in a split screen recording, a Discord call). A keyframeable view picks which region fills the frame, or every region shows at once in a grid. Each region has an offset that moves its picture and its sound in time, so a region recorded late can be lined up. Edit the regions in Effect Controls, place them on the picture with the Program monitor, and line them up with Sync regions.",
 "params": [
